    body: `Draw the land (ARCHITECTURE 6.4, DECISIONS 3; art direction docs/design-notes/look-and-sound.md section 2; budgets ARCHITECTURE 7).
- CDLOD terrain displaced on the GPU: one shared grid patch (e.g. 32x32 quads) drawn as instances (InstancedBufferGeometry, per-instance node x0, z0, size, level), one draw call (frustumCulled = false; you cull per node on the CPU). Quadtree from a 64 m level-0 node (2 m vertex spacing) up to the whole 1024 m zone; selection by distance with ranges giving a stable screen-space error, CPU frustum culling, written into a reused InstancedBufferAttribute each frame (no allocation). Vertex shader: height from u.uHeightTex via texelFetch with manual bilinear (R32F, NEAREST), CDLOD geomorphing of odd vertices toward the coarser grid near the node's range end, skirts on node edges so there are never cracks. Outside the zone, clamp to the edge or fall away smoothly into the deep (the ocean is opaque there).
- Fragment: normals from uHeightTex central differences at full resolution (crisp lighting at any LOD). Lambert via onBeforeCompile so shadows and fog work; add the shared uniforms with addWorldUniforms. A matching customDepthMaterial (same displacement) so terrain can cast shadows (use it when quality.shadows; never toggle renderer.shadowMap.enabled).
- Ground shading, world-space (no UVs; x/z-projected noise on steep faces), sin-free hashes in camera-relative coordinates (fp32 precision at 1 km), <= 6 hash evaluations per pixel near, <= 2 far:
  materials from groundTex/coverB: steep faces = rock; rock by kind (fresh basalt glossy blue-black -> matte -> grey-brown -> rusty with weathering coverB.r; placed Stone grey; Limestone cream); sand by kind (black / grey / gold / coral white) with wet darkening near the waterline and a little sparkle on dry sand up close; soil browns on flat ground where coverB.r is high (redder in the lee, dark humus under forest);
  lava from groundTex R (thickness) and G (heat): emissive glow ramp (deep red -> orange -> yellow -> near white), flow noise moving downhill, crust with glowing cracks below ~0.5 heat that narrow as it cools, a slow breathing pulse; u.uLavaGlow warmly lights nearby ground; lava stays bright at night (not fogged out);
  cover from coverA/B/C as patches that grow outward (noise thresholds, not uniform fades): lichen speckle (sage, pale yellow; orange near guano), moss velvet (brighter when moist coverB.b), grass (green; golden in the lee with u.uDry), forest-floor darkening (fake canopy shade) where coverA.a is high, guano whitewash on cliffs (coverB.g), burn char (coverB.a), streams/marsh glossy ribbons (coverC.a, animated downhill), coral/seagrass/coralline colours underwater (coverC);
  underwater: depth absorption toward teal/blue, caustics only within 6 m depth and 80 m of the camera (cheap), deep seabed cheap path; wet sheen after rain (u.uWet); fog from the shared uniforms.
- Make it beautiful: soft, sunny, cartoon-real Caribbean in the Sandcastle Cays family; readable as a living map from 800 m, rewarding up close at 20 m.
- Ponds (ponds.ts): one flat mesh per life.ponds entry at its level (from the life message via onEngine), transparent fresh (clear green-blue) or salt (milky, pinkish if the pink-pond effect species lives there - you can check life.pops for species with effect 'pink-pond'), small ripples, rain rings when u.uRain > 0, discard where ground is above the level; dispose meshes when ponds disappear.
- Budget: <= 150k terrain triangles in view on the phone (quality.phone), more on laptop; 1-2 draw calls (+1 shadow). Unit-test the CPU node selection (coverage without gaps, counts within budget at several camera poses, stable LOD) in tests/terrain.test.ts.
- Screenshots: god view of the whole zone, the volcano at 400 m, a beach at 40 m, a cliff at 60 m, underwater shallows; plus a lava test: --eval "window.__game.selectTool('lava')" then drive a stroke with window.__game.send({t:'stroke',phase:'start',tool:'lava',x:-60,z:40,radius:15,strength:1}) and screenshot a few seconds later (the stub engine makes lava appear and cool).`,
